+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 1941d806d2 (crbug 585624824)
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 27-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0012`). V8 15.6 1941d806d2
+(27-11; bugs 586790592 and 585624824; cherry-pick of main 686ea5103e; M159 twin 4ac3021e1e, 15.9.128.43).
+Applied as is to 15.6.75.66 (`js-call-reducer.cc` already had a FlyWeb patch, far from this hunk; the file's base
+blob matches upstream's). Severity not published.
+
+- The Array.prototype.sort that TurboFan inlines had no checkpoint between the loop headers and the comparefn call.
+  Eager deopts added when lowering the call (e.g. argument conversions for an inlined Wasm comparefn) used the frame
+  state from before the sort, so a deopt re-ran the sort after earlier comparefn calls had already run their side
+  effects (for instance, truncating the array).
+- Now a checkpoint with the sort's snapshot continuation (`SortContinueFromSnapshotEagerFrameState`) goes right before
+  the call. New test `mjsunit/regress/wasm/regress-585624824.js`.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`); no bytecode change.
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): build and run mjsunit `regress/wasm/regress-585624824` (with `--turbofan`), `compiler/*`,
+`wasm/*` and `regress/*`.
+
